          %h2#beck_modules Beck modules
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+modules"} Beck modules
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%5E%E2%88%9E-ring"} C^∞-ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the category of ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Stel"} Stel
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat+theories"} Fermat theories
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CR"} Carchedi–Roytenberg
          %p
            The proof proceeds like the proof given at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+module"} Beck module
            for ordinary rings, using the fact (
            %a{:href => "#DK"}> Dubuc–Kock
            , Proposition 1.2) that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideals"} ideals
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%5E%E2%88%9E-rings"} C^∞-rings
            coincide with ideals in the ordinary sense and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+zero+extension"} square zero extension
            construction used there can be promoted to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%5E%E2%88%9E-ring"} C^∞-ring
            using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+expansions"} Taylor expansions
            as explained in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DK"} Dubuc–Kock
          %p
            Furthermore, by
            %a{:href => "#DK"} Dubuc–Kock
            [Proposition 2.2] the resulting notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+derivation"} Beck derivation
            coincides with that of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%5E%E2%88%9E-derivation"} C^∞-derivation
            and by
            %a{:href => "#DK"} Dubuc–Kock
            [Theorem 2.3], the resulting module of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+derivations"} Beck derivations
            can be computed as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I/I^2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the kernel of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\otimes A\to A
          %h2#kainzkrieglmichor_modules Kainz–Kriegl–Michor modules
          %p A different, nonequivalent definition was proposed by Kainz–Kriegl–Michor in 1987.
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Poly
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Poly_k
            the following
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\to N
            are polynomial maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\to N
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym M^*\otimes_k N
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            can be identified with a product-preserving functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FinPoly
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinPoly_k\to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FinPoly
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinPoly_k
            is the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Poly
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Poly_k
            on finitely generated free modules. The value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(X)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi FinPoly
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in FinPoly_k
            can be thought of as the space of
            %span.newWikiWord
              regular functions
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/regular+functions"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A\to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            is the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Zariski spectrum
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Zariski+spectrum"} ?
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The starting observation is that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            over a commutative
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            can be identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dinatural+transformation"} dinatural transformation
            (dinatural in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartPoly
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in CartPoly
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi Poly
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta\colon Poly_k(X,M)\times A(X)\to M.
          %p
            We require
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            to be linear in the first argument.
          %p
            That is to say, to specify an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n\to M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n\to M
            with a
            %span.newWikiWord
              regular function
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/regular+function"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A\to k^n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A\to M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            as the module of sections of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaf
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A\to M
            can be restricted to the diagonal
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            as required.
          %p
            The proposal of Kainz–Kriegl–Michor is then to replace polynomial maps with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+maps"} smooth maps
          %p
            A
            %strong C^∞-module
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%5E%E2%88%9E-ring"} C^∞-ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a Hausdorff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+topological+vector+space"} locally convex topological vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            together with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dinatural+transformation"} dinatural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta\colon C^\infty(X,M)\times A(X)\to M
          %p
            that is linear in the first argument. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is also continuous in the first argument, we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong continuous C^∞-module
          %p
            Topological vector spaces in the above definition can be replaced by any notion of a vector space that allows for smooth maps, e.g.,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+vector+space"} convenient vector space
            etc.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+module"}> Beck module
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+derivation"} Beck derivation
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#DK
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+J.+Dubuc"}> E. J. Dubuc
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Kock"} A. Kock
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On 1-form classifiers
                %strong 12
                12 (1984) 1471-1531 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/00927878408823064"}> doi:10.1080/00927878408823064
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Stel
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Stel"}> Herman Stel
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                    \-Stacks and their Function Algebras with applications to
                    = succeed "-Lie" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "/schreiber/files/StelThesisB.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Stel"} webpage
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Carchedi"}> David Carchedi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"} Dmitry Roytenberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homological Algebra for Superalgebras of Differentiable Functions
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1212.3745"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                G. Kainz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Kriegl"} Andreas Kriegl
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Michor"} Peter Michor
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
                    \-algebras from the functional analytic view point
                %strong 46
                1 (1987) 89-107 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(87)90045-4"} doi:10.1016/0022-4049(87)90045-4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~michor/c-oo-alg.pdf"} pdf
        .revisedby
          %p
